<title>THAILAND: Asia Credit signs 10 bln yen 3-yr loan.</title>
<headline>Asia Credit signs 10 bln yen 3-yr loan.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asia Credit Plc said on Thursday it had signed a 10 billion yen three-year syndicated loan from 13 leading international banks.</p>
<p>The loan carries a margin of 60 basis points over yen LIBOR.</p>
<p>Asia Credit said the funds would be used for general funding purposes.</p>
<p>The syndication was arranged by BA Asia, Societe Generale Asia and Sumitomo Bank.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
